Do you still mean=20
"SUMTI is individual" =3Dca'e {RO DA poi ke'a me SUMTI zo'u SUMTI me DA}
with the term "individual"?

If so, keeping {lo broda} to be individual requires attentiveness on the=20
universe of discourse, and reduces the flexibility of the language.

Let me give an example.

lo prenu cu jmaji gi'e jukpa gi'e citka

I want to mean with this sentence that this {lo prenu} consists of at least=
=20
two persons {by} and {cy}, and satisfies {jmaji} collectively {je}=20
non-distributively, {jukpa} collectively {ja} distributively, {citka}=20
non-collectively {je} distributively. This {lo} cannot be replaced by {loi}=
=20
because I want it to satisfy a selbri non-collectively.

For this {lo prenu}, {by me lo prenu} is true, but {lo prenu me by} is=20
false, so this {lo prenu} is not individual.
It is still possible that you don't include {by} and {cy} in your universe=
=20
of discourse and say that {lo prenu} is individual, but it is your=20
epistemology, and not defined by the language.

=20

